  "description": "The best deviled eggs are creamy, savory, punchy, and light, made with good Dijon mustard, homemade mayo, and good olive oil.",
  "notes": "Optional substitutions: Crushed red pepper → hot paprika\n\nNotes: For the best results, use really, really good olive oil.\nI like overstuffing the eggs, which leaves you with a few extra whites. Just eat 'em (or feed them to the dog). Eggs that are a couple of weeks old will peel more easily than very fresh eggs.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: You can boil the eggs and make the filling one day ahead of time.",
